// Title: Potential RjvPlatform.DLL Sideloading From Default Location
// Sigma ID: 259dda31-b7a3-444f-b7d8-17f96e8a7d0d
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: X__Junior (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-06-09 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: persistence, privilege-escalation, execution, stealth, T1574.001
// Description: Detects loading of "RjvPlatform.dll" by the "SystemResetPlatform.exe" binary which can be abused
//   as a method of DLL side loading since the "$SysReset" directory isn't created by default.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/0gtweet/status/1666716511988330499
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/image_load/image_load_side_load_rjvplatform_default_location.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceImageLoadEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath =~ "C:\\Windows\\System32\\SystemResetPlatform\\SystemResetPlatform.exe" and FolderPath =~ "C:\\$SysReset\\Framework\\Stack\\RjvPlatform.dll"
